{
  "id": "COMPOUND:27653 - PROTEIN:5845",
  "verbalization": "Prejadomycin is implicated in the regulation of SNU1 through a series of mechanistic pathways. The evidence suggests that Prejadomycin acts as a target for VMRC-LCP, which is subsequently targeted by Neridienone A. This cascade leads to the activation of SNU1, indicating a potential role in the biological process of SNU1 regulation. Similarly, Prejadomycin is also linked to Hepatocyte, which is targeted by Neridienone A, further reinforcing the involvement of this pathway in SNU1 regulation. The consistent presence of Neridienone A as a mediator in both pathways underscores the importance of this compound in the relationship between Prejadomycin and SNU1. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Prejadomycin influences SNU1, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
